Moreinfo:
AP & AO career spans 12 years of experience in manufacturing, retail and service industries, outsourcing, IT (1> year).
KEY SKILLS AND COMPETENCES:
	- Strong Microsoft Office skills; Xero, SAP, 1C; proficient in Excel (pivot tables); Power BI, Google docs, SharePoint, OneDrive.
	- Excellent analytical, reconciliation and overall troubleshooting skills.
	- Compliance and participation in the development and writing of operating procedures.

RESPONSIBILITIES: 
•	AR – invoices (creation, updating, editing, cooperation with sales team and customers, remittance advices, control of receivables (overdue invoices);
•	AP – posting bills, cooperation with vendors, supplier payment list;
•	FA – register, disposal, run monthly depreciation;
•	Debit/credit card operations, transaction reconciliation (Pleo, PayPal, Merchant Checkout, Cardstream, Barclaycard);
•	Bank statements
•	Monthly reconciliation of balance sheet accounts.
•	Maintaining general ledger and preparing journal entries, posting accruals and monthly expenses;
•	Administration of accounting periods closing (monthly, quarterly, annual PEC)
•	Communication with main accountants from Eastern Europe for elimination of deviations and discrepancies.

I would like to occupy a middle range position in a company that is keen on hiring individuals who are smart, financially aware and tend to personal development and growth. My ideal responcibilities scope : general accountancy + finance analysis

candidate_profile:
Position:
CFO, Finance Director, Deputy Finance Director

Moreinfo:
Finance and Reporting:
•	running and coordinating the process of month-end closing and financial reporting process (18 entities);
•	leading the reporting month and year close process for multiple entities (P&L, BS, CF);
•	coordinating communication between different departments and head office;
•	coordinating cost allocation and reconciliation between entities; 
•	providing consistent application of accounting rules within the region and IFRS standards;
•	coordinating timeline and availability of resources to perform regular group audits.
Budgeting and forecasting:
•	running the process of budgeting and forecasting;
•	design and implementing of budget control mechanisms;
•	managing operational data and ensuring data integrity and accuracy for reporting and budgeting process;
•	providing effective financial support and identifying any key risks;
Tax compliance and controls:
•	running internal tax audits for all entities;
•	recommend and implementing efficient tax reports review and preparation processes;
•	working with external consultants in order to find out the best option tax issues;
•	reviewing agreements and commercial deals according to internal approval matrix;
Treasury and accounting:
•	perform all negotiations concerning financing and banking agreements in Ukraine;
•	directing cash management and financial risk management;
•	support the audit process.

