candidate_profile:
Position:
Communications manager, Internal communications manager

Moreinfo:
Once upon a time I've been a lawyer.
But then communications won.

So far that was a beautiful nine years journey (and ongoing) with teams of different types and scales.

Upon this road, I did my best to “boost” myself as a creator and team leader by learning how to tell &listen to stories, to trust&build trust in return, how to collaborate&delegate. That was a story about being brave where needed, making hard decisions, finding alternative scenarios (when smth goes in the way not expected).

A pretty “eclectic” work path brought me an understanding of how different types of organizations live, develop, and change. I’ve got a chance to “feel” the spirit and vibes of the startup world, nonprofits, public sector, impact tech, agencies field, and social projects. This mix stayed in my mind, heart, and soul to solve puzzles of further challenges. 

Using emotional intelligence, empathy, and respect as main working tools.

Looking For:
A SENIOR POSITION OF PROJECT MANAGER OR COMMUNICATIONS LEAD (PREFERABLY INTERNAL COMMS) AT IMPACTFUL PROJECT TO JOINTLY CREATE STORIES THAT TRULY MATTERS

Highlights:
Promoting a culture of blended education  at Ukrainian edu tech startup MOOCology;

Pitching at least 500 times in more than 7 countries and launching pivots in Ukraine, Poland, and the Czech Republic for Ukrainian startup on parking search Tap4Parking. Winning second place in the incubation program for our pitch;

Working on international communications within Eurovision 2017 campaign;  

Helping New Era Orchestra to fundraise for a trip to Septembre music festival to present Ukrainian classical music on the stage for the first time in the history of the festival;

Working with hromadas to develop their comms skills to boost their investment attractiveness;

Doing fun and crazy things like brochures for children on how to become an MP while working with the Parliament of Ukraine and Vice Prime Minister’s (VPM) office for EU and NATO integration; 

Promoting civic tech in Ukraine, mentoring gov and impact tech startups

English Level:
fluent

Experience Years:
8.0

CV:
Promoting a culture of blended education  at Ukrainian edu tech startup MOOCology;

Pitching at least 500 times in more than 7 countries and launching pivots in Ukraine, Poland, and the Czech Republic for Ukrainian startup on parking search Tap4Parking. Winning second place in the incubation program for our pitch;

Working on international communications within Eurovision 2017 campaign;  

Helping New Era Orchestra to fundraise for a trip to Septembre music festival to present Ukrainian classical music on the stage for the first time in the history of the festival;

Working with hromadas to develop their comms skills to boost their investment attractiveness;

Doing fun and crazy things like brochures for children on how to become an MP while working with the Parliament of Ukraine and Vice Prime Minister’s (VPM) office for EU and NATO integration; 

Promoting civic tech in Ukraine, mentoring gov and impact tech startups
