candidate_profile:
Position:
Automation QA Engineer

Moreinfo:
More then 15 years of IT experience; 

Working as QA engineer on a microservices based high-load web application;

Leading QA team of three manual test engineers. Interviewing new employees. Mentoring and coordination of manual and automation testing processes, individual development plan design. Took part in the company’s internal development processes setting up;

Planning and design of a testing strategy, tests results reporting. Design review, manual and automated tests execution, test documentation design(test cases, checklists, traceability matrix);

Assist software engineers in troubleshooting problems in development and production. Tasks assignment between team members;

Automated testing using JS/Ruby + Selenium WebDriver + Rspec, Chai with version control tools (Git); with bug-tracking systems JIRA;

Setting up the continuous integration process. Creating pipelines ‘Build - Test - Report’ for different test packages, environments, conditions;

Maintenance of the Git CI runner;

RESTful web services testing manual testing using CURL and Postman;

Good analytical and critical thinking skills;

Bug root cause discovering, bug prioritization, bug registration/verification;

Requirements analysis/testing.  Specification creation;

Communication with customers to requirements clarifying.

Looking For:
I want to get the position of QA Automation Engineer to apply my skills and knowledge in manual testing and in automation testing.
I want to find interesting project with the opportunity of automation testing (API+UI).
I want to work in a highly qualified team, where I will have the opportunity for professional realization and growth.

