candidate_profile:
Position:
Business Analyst/Product owner

Moreinfo:
I've been working as a business analyst for almost 3 years on various projects (enterprise, discovery phases, presale projects). 
My latest project was for one of the largest media companies; together with the team, we were building a document processing pipeline based on AWS lambdas with minimal UI for Content operators (Lawyers) from scratch. 
Earlier in my experience, I was working for a large company that is focused on developing Robotic Process Automation software. For the first milestone, we did a redesign of the UI for the whole system using the component library to make all the company's products consistent. For the second milestone, we were decoupling the architecture from monolith to microservice architecture.

My responsibilities and achievements are: 
- Creating the roadmap for the team and stakeholders for 2 releases ahead;
- Delivering the project within the approved roadmap, constraints, clarifying requirements; 
- Prioritizing requirements according to stakeholder needs and technical aspects added by the delivery team;
- Translating requirements to the agile teams in a form of epics, user stories with acceptance criteria, SRS documents, BRD;
- Reviewing and contributing to the technical documentation of the product (mapping documents, architecture diagrams);
- Facilitating SCRUM meetings; 
- Reporting to the higher management regarding team performance and pace;
- Shaping and maintaining teams' spring and release backlogs; 
- Modelling using BPMN and UML; 
- Prototyping in Figma or Azure RP; 
- Product and market research for decision making background;

Looking For:
No gaming or gambling projects.

Highlights:
Built a roadmap for the team who never worked with the business analyst before. Delivered first release within scope, time, and budget. 
Offered lots of UX solutions during the redesign of the system, proactively contacted stakeholders during the redesign phase to review and approve solutions.

English Level:
fluent

Experience Years:
3.0

