Responsibilities:
- Work with product manager and stakeholders in terms of business needs, requirements, functionality and improvement opportunities;
- Elicitation, analysis and documentation of software requirements into detailed specifications in the form of user stories and acceptance criteria;
- Work break structure preparation for the requirements and acceptance criteria defining;
- Discussion and estimation of requirements with the team;
- Documentation and managing requirements according to Legal regulations;
- Consultation of development/test teams during the implementation phase (validation of implemented results and resolve any issues faced by the team);
- Preparing UML diagram (Use case diagram, Activities diagram);
- Identification and resolution of issues with conflicting requirements;
- Facilitation of Agile ceremonies (dailys, planning, grooming, review)
- Participation in product testing;
- Stakeholders management;
- Requirements gathering and analysis;
- Ensure that documents produced keep technology aligned with project objectives;
- Collaborate with developers to establish the technical vision and analyze usability and performance needs;
- Customer communication and consultancy;
- Participate in technical pre-sales with customers;
- Translating the needs of different stakeholders into concrete business requirements;
- Co-create solutions with various stakeholders and come up with innovative ideas;
- Analyze and digest business requirements into technical stories ready to be developed;
- Explain complex solutions to business and non-technical people;
- Pre-sale activities: Discovery phase, Projects estimation, preparing commercial proposal;

Moreinfo:
I build teams who can make software running in the Cloud under high load.

- 10 years of experience in IT, 8+ of which as a full-time Business/System Analyst 
- Bachelor in CS, Master's in System Analysis 
- Domains: Telecom, eCommerce, AdTech, Manufacturing, Web, Mobile; familiar with Cloud (AWS)
- Performed roles: Technical Writer, System Analyst, Business Analyst, Technical Product Owner, Scrum Master.
- Coordinated work of backend, web and mobile teams (Android, IOS).
- 5 successfully delivered large scale projects.

Today I help a US-based public company run a team of 8-10 engineers as a Scrum Master.  program with multiple initiatives to decompose a monolithic, up-and-running system into microservices to achieve scalability and enable the company’s global expansion.

What I do:
- collaborate with business & end users to elicit the needs & set expectations;
- collaborate with Product, UI/UX & architecture in terms of a technical solution, limitations & NFRs;
- translate PRD into Jira tasks, write stories and ACs;
- manage Jira backlog;
- drive Scrum ceremonies;
- resolve blockers;
- coordinate cross-team dependencies within the program and their alignment to the release schedule of an organization overall;
- manage releases.

I am seeking an opportunity to transition to Product Management. I will be an excellent addition to your team if you're looking for someone with a technical background.

candidate_profile:
Position:
Chief Technical Officer | Head of Engineering

Moreinfo:
I have experience in technical development and launch of business products, as well as experience in financial planning, strategic planning, business development and project management. I lead a development team and integrate Agile methodologies. Engaged in the implementation of innovations, process optimization and provision of high-quality software solutions. I have a wide range of technologies, a solid foundation for software development, architecture selection and security standards.

Can be distinguished:
Hiring and managing the development team;
Ensuring high code quality and following programming best practices;
Support of a high level of product security according to OWASP and PCI DSS standards;
Implementation of new technologies and methodologies to improve the development process;
Development and optimization of product architecture;
More than 12 years of experience as a software developer (PHP);
Of them, experience in the role of Team Lead is 6 years;
Project Manager skills, use PMBoK and actively implement into existing processes;
Deep understanding of SDLC processes and development methodologies;
Implementation and support of Agile culture in the team;
Evaluation of projects, understanding of the client's needs, proposals of realistic and effective solutions, both for the client and for the company;
The ability to see promising and non-promising projects;
Ability to grow personnel, personal mentoring;
Ability to explain complex technical issues in simple words, critical analysis of projects and decomposition into understandable tasks, analysis of customer tasks before starting work;
Strong problem solving skills and attention to detail;
Preparation of technical documentation and road maps for the team;
Ensuring consistency of technical projects with the company's business goals.

Skills:
Business and planning: Financial planning, Strategic planning · Business development;
Leadership and team management: JIRA, Asana, Agile, SDLC, Lean, CI/CD, TOC, Scrum, LeSS, Kanban, WBS, DISC, RACI;
Infrastructure: Linux Server, Windows Server, GCP, AWS, Azure, VMware, KVM, Docker, Microservices, Zabbix;
Databases: MongoDB, MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite;
Testing: BrowserStack, Selenium, PHPUnit, Protractor, Karma;
Security: PCI DSS, OWASP, SAST, DAST;
Other: Linux, Nginx, Apache, PHP, SOLID, OOD/OOP, Patterns, Yii2, Laravel, Symfony, REST API, SQL, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, SASS/SCSS, Less, Bootstrap, jQuery, React, Vue.js.

