candidate_profile:
Position:
Chief specialist of the Department of International Transfers

Moreinfo:
Practical experience:
- Business process architecture design;
- Designing the architecture of Information computer systems;
- Creation of payment products, services (OpenAPI, API Gateways and Microservices), WEB GUI;
- Integration of external services into Internet banking (front & back).

Key skills:
- Business process modeling notation (BPMN 2.0/UML);
- Distributed systems. Design patterns;
- Integration protocols (HTTP, REST, SOAP);
- Data transfer formats (XML,JSON);
- Databases (SQL,NoSQL);
- Event systems: Kafka, RabbitMQ;
- Network technologies;
- E-antifraud systems (online payments, compliance);
- DevOps;
- BigData;
- Node-Red;
- Audit of the IT infrastructure;
- Data mapping;
- Design of architectural solutions for business processes, IS and DB;
- UX/UI design;
- Automation of business processes;
- Project management;
- PM tools (Jira, Git, Confluence);
- Stakeholder management;
- System testing;
- Risk management in projects;
- Flexible software development methodologies (Agile, Scrum);
- Deep understanding of SDLC

Projects:
 Implementation of the new standard of SWIFT messages - ISO 20022 and
creation of a new architecture of the business process for processing
incoming/outgoing payments in intrabank IS/involved divisions;
 Creation of a technological process for obtaining, saving, and imposing the
client's electronic signature on the applications of money transfer systems;
 Development of the architecture of the technical process for automatic
generation of the NBU E-limit;
 Integration of the Payoneer service into Privat24;
 Implementation of a transactional website for sending Western Union
transfers;
 Creation of counters in P2P transfers;
 Creation of a new UX/UI of money transfers for TSO; Implementation of the new version of send/payout transfers to Privat24;
 Implementation of the project "Sending Swift payments in the Privat24
application";
 Transfers by phone number to other banks;
 Implementation of DirectCard technology and integration with money transfer
systems;
 Creation of processes in Node-Red;
 Implementation of the possibility of sending SWIFT payments with the function
of auto-conversion;
 Parsing and gathering information from target sites;
 Implementation of file content analysis technology (text or image) using
BigData technologies;
 Creation of efficiency dashboards in terms of products of the Department;

Highlights:
Awards:
- For successful implementation of the new version of send/payout transfers to Privat24 (2021);
