Skills and experience in C++ (summary of 10 years: scientific applications development, development training for engineering students). 

Levels: 
- C++ - advanced (C++ 03/11, experience in development of scientific data processing/simulation applications);
- VCL - intermediate/advanced (in both C++ Builder and Delphi/Lazarus environments);
- Qt: intermediate/basic (1 year of non-industrial experience according to scientific activities);
- Python: basic/intermediate (pre-certified: GeekBrains), no industrial experience;

Other skills: 
- Research (fluent, 10 full years of experience in applied mechanics/robotics/mechanical engineering)
- Analytical thinking, systematization of knowledge;
- Mathematics: special course of mathematical analysis, Bauman University;
- English: IELTS 6.0 (IELTS program, DeMontfort university English Language test);

Possibilities:
- Searching for relocation outside Russia.

Looking For:
Interesting projects;
Financial stability;
Flexible working schedule and the possibility to work remotely

It could be product, outsourcing or outstaffing company. I expect:
-- your company makes money for it offers good services, not for your false advertisement for a product that does not exist;

-- when one says good services, one does mean that this or that product makes someone's life easier, say, in studying, healthcare, business, daily routine, i.e. living;

-- if there is something that needs to be sold at all, it is to be that thing which will have a buyer actually benefit from it, which definitely not casino or stuff alike;

-- if the product considers itself a respectful one towards those who would use it, it is to make sure it 's not wasting time upon one opening it.

Highlights:
-- collected 133 000 UAH at once even though the person had not been willing to pay 10 000 UAH at first even;

-- being a customer care agent, people would tend to ask me to deal with their clients for my proclivity towards politeness & compassion during conversations;

-- critical thinking & profiling skills--the latter has been taught in "Corporate Security Research Centre"

