candidate_profile:
Position:
AUTOSAR Classic developer/ Automotive Embedded

Moreinfo:
Experience in Automotive domain, AUTOSAR Classic subdomain. Have skills in electronics: reading circuits, soldering, working with a multimeter, signal analyzer, oscilloscope. Have a basic knowledge in TCP/IP networks (including Cyclone TCP stack) and in MBSD approach (Matlab/Simulink/Embedded Coder/AUTOSAR Toolbox).

Technical skills:

Compilers:
- Arm GNU Toolchain;
- GNU GCC;
- Green Hills.

MCUs:
- STM32;
- Renesas RH850/ R-Car H3;
- Arduino;
- TI C2000.

Development tools:
- MS Visual Studio;
- TI Code Composer Studio;
- Renesas CS+;
- STM32CubeIDE/CubeMX;
- VS Code;
- Eclipse IDE;
- HighTec IDE;
- Matlab & Simulink & Embedded Coder & AUTOSAR Toolbox;
- Vector DaVinci Configurator;
- Vector DaVinci Developer;
- Vector CANoe;
- Vector VTT;
- Vector CANdbc++;
- Make;

Debugging & Measurement tools:
- Lauterbach / TRACE32;
- ST-Link;
- Multimeter;
- Renesas Emulator;
- Vector CANoe/VN1630A;
- Wireshark;
- Logic analyzer;
- PicoScope/Oscilloscope;

Requirements & Architecture tools:
- IBM Doors;
- IBM Rhapsody;
- Enterprise Architect;

Embedded interfaces:
- Intra-connected: SPI, I2C;
- Inter-connected: UART, CAN, LIN, Ethernet;

Testing Tools:
- Cantata;
- Vector CANoe;
- Ceedling;

Project infrastructure:
- Confluence;
- Jira;
- Jenkins;
- Git/Gerrit/GitHub.

Methodologies:
- ASPICE;
- SCRUM.

Experience:

1. Compressor motor ECU:
    - Development a framework for integration tests;

  2. Automatic Transmission for a Germany OEM: 
    - Integrating MCAL drivers;
    - Board bring-up;
    - Integration and AUTOSAR BSW configuration (ASPICE SWE.5);

  3. Mentoring (AUTOSAR Classic).

  4. Automotive gateway for a Germany OEM:
    - Analysis and development of system requirements (ASPICE SYS.2); 
    - Architecture designing (ASPICE SWE.2);
    - Detailed architecture designing (ASPICE SWE.3).

  5. Head unit development for the Asian OEM:
    - Development of CDD components (AUTOSAR);
    - Integration and Unit testing.

