candidate_profile:
Position:
Business Analyst

Moreinfo:
Junior business analyst: 
Participated in Business Analysis Global Mentoring Program.

Topics, which were covered and practiced during the course:
Agile & Waterfall methods;
Scrum essentials;
Stakeholder analysis, stakeholder management;
Types of requirements;
Requirements elicitation techniques;
Requirements documentation;
Requirements quality;
Prioritization techniques;
Modeling and diagrams (BPMN, Use Case diagram, Activity diagram, Sequence
diagrams);
Prototyping and tools;
Business analysis information management (JIRA, CONFLUENCE);
Basic knowledge of SQL;
Risk Management.

Administrative assistant: 
My responsibilities include:

Work with CONFLUENCE, JIRA (editing and writing needed information about Ukraine's offices EPAM);
work with onboarding process;
plan the team building for all Administrative team;
work in all company's portals (desk; telescope; vacation; support);
prepare NDA & Offers for students: 
business communication through mails (Teams, Outlook);
writing mailings;
make some presentations of different projects (as a result of work on the project);
preparation meetings|calls with all administrative team;
do all tasks of my RM;
work with Excel, the entire documentation record goes through it;
communicate with all departments;
work in Microsoft Word;
maintaining and scheduling meeting rooms;
ordering supplies;
work with the courier. Plan a schedule for couriers for the whole day.
send mails to other cities/countries;
provide any help to colleagues within the framework of work duties.

Lead Generation Manager
My responsibilities included:

searching clients for the projects;
writing letters/applications;
writing templates and answers to questions, which could ask potential clients; 
introduction of negotiations with customers;
keep a table of performed work;
doing tasks from my manager.

